{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1491","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1491","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1491\",\"parent_revision\":\"cd301fb7a07a4d35323a44524f638f12ff5720b5524d286ce8959a97dc980e50\",\"root_revision\":\"cd301fb7a07a4d35323a44524f638f12ff5720b5524d286ce8959a97dc980e50\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe TaskBackend Protocol method append_task_section(plan_id, task_id, section_name, content) silently drops content in LocalYamlTaskProvider when section_name is not a named TaskData field (context_notes, body, handoff, etc.). The YAML writer routes writes by field name; an unrecognized name produces no error and no warning \u2014 the content is silently discarded. The Protocol signature and the architect spec do not document this constraint. Any agent or consumer calling append_task_section with a generic section name (e.g. \\\"Findings\\\", \\\"Work Log\\\") will lose data with no indication of failure. Observed during T06 conformance test implementation: the parametrized test required using section_name=\\\"context_notes\\\" rather than an arbitrary string to exercise the concrete behavior consistently across both LocalYamlTaskProvider and InMemoryTaskProvider backends.\\n\\nVerbatim user report: The T06 agent discovered that append_task_section(plan_id, task_id, section_name, content) in LocalYamlTaskProvider only works if section_name is a named TaskData field (context_notes, body, handoff, etc.). If a caller passes an arbitrary string like \\\"Findings\\\" or \\\"Work Log\\\", the YAML writer routes by field name, finds no match, and silently drops the content \u2014 no error, no warning. The Protocol signature doesn't say this. The architect spec doesn't document this constraint. Any agent that calls append_task_section with a freeform name will lose data and have no idea.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **append_task_section silently drops content when section_name is not a named taskdata field** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Implementation observation \u2014 T06 conformance test, P912 session 2026-04-05\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4e1beaf93c6d7ceb757b8723737bd4a2fa6fa37295268da781a3636ec48e1197\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCwQuQ\"}"}